# Branch & PR Automation

## Install

Copy this whole folder to `.github/skills/branch-and-pr-automation/` at the
repository root (the folder name must stay `branch-and-pr-automation` — it
has to match the `name` field above). VS Code discovers it automatically;
invoke it with `/branch-and-pr-automation` or let Copilot auto-load it when a
request matches the description above.

## When to use this skill

- "Create a branch and push these changes"
- "Push to testbranch and open a PR"
- "Branch off and raise a pull request"

## 0. Fidelity Ledger

| Concern | Authoritative tool | Rejected alternative | Why rejected |
|---|---|---|---|
| Branch/commit/push mutations | `git` CLI | Editor Source Control GUI | Not scriptable/headless for agent mode; no deterministic exit codes |
| PR creation & metadata | `gh` CLI (GitHub CLI) | Raw REST calls via `curl` + PAT | Duplicates auth handling `gh` already does correctly; higher error surface |
| Base branch detection | `gh repo view --json defaultBranchRef` + `git branch` | Assuming `main` by convention | Repos vary (`main`, `master`, `develop`); guessing violates evidence-only principle |
| Change description content | `git diff --stat`, `git log <base>..testbranch` | Free-form summary of "what was probably intended" | Must cite exact files/commits, never guessed intent |

**Scope boundary — prompt injection:** this skill operates only on the developer's own local repo and commit history (trusted input). No external contributor content is processed, so no injection guard is included. If this skill is ever pointed at a fork/external PR body as input, that guard must be added first.

