## Phase 0 — Certification Harness (hard gate, 8/8 required)

Run [preflight-check.sh](./scripts/preflight-check.sh) before anything else:

```bash
bash .github/skills/branch-and-pr-automation/scripts/preflight-check.sh testbranch
```

It checks, in order: git availability, that you're inside a git repo, `gh` auth, remote reachability, push permission (best-effort), working-tree status, `testbranch` name collisions (local + remote), and current branch/HEAD SHA. Any hard-blocking failure (checks 1–4) aborts with the exact evidence — do not proceed to Phase 1 on a non-zero exit.

---

## Phase 1 — Base Branch Confirmation (mandatory human gate)

Never assume the base branch. Build the candidate list only from Phase 0 evidence plus:

```bash
gh repo view --json defaultBranchRef --jq .defaultBranchRef.name
```

Present exactly this and stop until the user responds:

```
CONFIRMATION REQUIRED — no branch will be created until you confirm.

Create `testbranch` from which base?
  1. <current-branch>   (currently checked out, HEAD <sha>)
  2. <default-branch>   (repository default)
  3. Other — specify a branch name

Reply with 1, 2, or 3+name.
```

Record the confirmed base branch and its HEAD SHA (`git rev-parse <base>`) — this anchors Phase 5's diff evidence.

---

## Phase 2 — Collision Check & Branch Creation

Using the Phase 0 collision evidence:

- **No collision:**
  ```bash
  git checkout <confirmed-base>
  git pull origin <confirmed-base>
  git checkout -b testbranch
  ```
- **Local collision:** ask — reuse existing local `testbranch` (rebase onto confirmed base) / delete and recreate / choose a different name. Never auto-delete.
- **Remote collision:** ask — push on top of the existing remote `testbranch` / delete the remote branch first / choose a different name. Never force-delete a remote branch without a confirmation that names that exact action.

Post-condition: `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` must equal `testbranch` before continuing.

---

## Phase 3 — Change Evidence Capture & Commit

```bash
git status --porcelain
git diff --stat
```

- Both empty → `Not detected — no staged/unstaged changes found via git status --porcelain`. Abort; nothing to push.
- Otherwise:
  ```bash
  git add -A
  git commit -m "<generated message>"
  ```
- **Commit message rule:** built only from the `git diff --stat` file list and change type (added/modified/deleted) — no inferred rationale. Example: `Update auth/session.py, add auth/tests/test_session.py (3 files changed, +142/-18)`.

---

## Phase 4 — Push to Remote

```bash
git push -u origin testbranch
```

Non-fast-forward/rejected push → stop, show the exact `git` error, ask the user how to proceed. Never `--force` without a separate confirmation that names force-push specifically. Verify: `git ls-remote origin testbranch` SHA must match local `git rev-parse testbranch`.

---

## Phase 5 — PR Creation (evidence-only description)

Generate the body with [generate-pr-body.sh](./scripts/generate-pr-body.sh):

```bash
bash .github/skills/branch-and-pr-automation/scripts/generate-pr-body.sh <confirmed-base> testbranch > /tmp/pr-body.md
```

This produces `Summary`, `Changes Made` (per-file, from `--name-status`), `Commits` (from `git log`), `Testing`, and `Related Issues` (auto-detected `#123`-style refs from commit messages, or an explicit "Not detected" line) — every line traces to real diff/log output.

Create the PR:
```bash
gh pr create --base <confirmed-base> --head testbranch \
  --title "<generated from diff --stat summary>" \
  --body-file /tmp/pr-body.md
```

---

## Phase 6 — Post-Creation Verification

```bash
gh pr view <number> --json url,state,baseRefName,headRefName
```

Confirm `baseRefName` == confirmed base, `headRefName` == `testbranch`, `state` == `OPEN`. Report to the user: PR URL, PR number, base branch, files changed count, commit count.

---

## Rollback / Failure Handling

At every phase, on any command failure: stop immediately, show the exact command and its exact error output, do not attempt an automatic alternate path, and suggest specific manual remediation (e.g., `git branch -D testbranch` to undo a bad local create). No phase silently continues past a failed prior phase.

## Known Limitations (honest fidelity tradeoffs)

- Does not resolve merge conflicts if `testbranch` diverges from base after creation — flags for manual resolution rather than auto-merging.
- Assumes a single remote named `origin`; multi-remote repos require an explicit `--repo` override to `gh`.
- Assumes `gh auth login` has already been completed interactively; this skill does not perform first-time OAuth setup.
- Fixed branch name `testbranch` is per spec — collision handling exists, but no auto-suffixing (e.g., `testbranch-2`) happens without explicit user confirmation.

